{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>When the flesh of his foreskin is circumcised.</b> As he was commanded above, ״ונמלתם את בשר ערלתכם״ — and it shall be a sign of the covenant. And He explained to us that the commandment is a fixed sign in the flesh, and the flesh is a sign of the covenant; therefore this commandment is called an אות (sign). And three commandments in the Torah are called אות, and they are: מילה (circumcision), שבת (Sabbath), and תפילין (phylacteries) — and all three are testimony and a sign concerning the unity and the faith. And it is not fitting for any individual of Israel to stand without two of them, for the establishment of every matter requires two witnesses; and accordingly two witnesses must accompany him. Therefore a person is obligated to be scrupulous in the commandment of תפילין, and then his two witnesses will never depart from him. As that sage who prided himself in them said: 'All my days I never walked four cubits without Torah and without תפילין.' And on the day of Shabbat, when he is exempt from תפילין, מילה and שבת are found in him — teaching that whoever is scrupulous in the commandment of תפילין, his two witnesses never depart from him forever, neither on a weekday nor on Shabbat." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״בהמולו בשר ערלתו״ — great is circumcision, for whoever is circumcised does not descend to Gehenna. It is written here: ״ביום ההוא כרת ה׳ את אברם ברית,״ and it is written there (Leviticus 12:3): ״וביום השמיני ימול.״ And who descends to Gehenna? One concerning whom it is written afterward: ״את הקיני ואת הקנזי ואת הקדמוני״ — for all of them are uncircumcised of heart, and all the wicked descend to Gehena. Thus we find in Ezekiel (Ezekiel 32:18): ״בן אדם נהה על המון מצרים והורידהו,״ שם אשור וכל קהלה, שם משך תובל וכל המונה — all of them ערלים (uncircumcised), מחללי חרב (pierced by the sword); שמה נסיכי צפון. And so Isaiah said (Isaiah 5:14): ״לכן הרחיבה שאול נפשה ופערה פיה לבלי חק״ — to whom does it open its mouth? To those who have no חק (statute), as it is said (Psalms 105:10): ״ויעמידה ליעקב לחק.״ And the verse further says (Zechariah 9:11): ״גם את בדם בריתך שלחתי אסיריך מבור אין מים בו,״ and it is written (Proverbs 31:21): ״לא תירא לביתה משלג כי כל ביתה לבוש שנים״ — end of quotation. And therefore all Israel have the practice of circumcising the deceased child who did not reach the age for the commandment of מילה — they circumcise him at the grave." "<b>Israel merited</b> this commandment, for it is firmly held in their hand, and through it they were promised three gifts: the kingdom of the house of David, that it shall never be cut off; the gift of the Land, that it shall be theirs as an eternal possession; and the Shekhinah, that it shall dwell among Israel. And all three are alluded to in this parashah. The kingdom of the house of David — as He said: ״ונתתיך לגוים ומלכים ממך יצאו,״ and this verse is in the context of the covenant. And we find regarding the kingdom of the house of David a covenant, as it is written (Psalms 89): ״כרתי ברית לבחירי נשבעתי לדוד עבדי, עד עולם אכין זרעך ובניתי לדור ודור כסאך סלה.״ The gift of the Land — as He said: ״ונתתי לך ולזרעך אחריך את ארץ מגוריך את כל ארץ כנען לאחוזת עולם.״ He explained that the Land shall be an eternal possession for Israel — that none other shall inherit it and none other shall settle it, only they; and if perchance they are exiled from it, they shall return to it, for it is an eternal possession for them, not for the gentiles. And this is a great sign for Israel: that from the day they were exiled from it, no nation at all settled there; rather it remained desolate and devastated until her children return to her. The Shekhinah that shall dwell among Israel — as He said: ״והייתי להם לאלהים,״ that is, to them alone and not to the gentiles. And happy is the people that was promised three such gifts: the kingdom of the house of David, that it shall never be cut off forever; that the Holy Land shall be theirs alone as a gift for an eternal possession; and that the Shekhinah shall dwell among them — something no nation among the gentiles merited, not even one of all these. And this is what David said (Psalms 144:15): ״אשרי העם שככה לו אשרי העם שה׳ אלהיו.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The idiom לנער המת שלא הגיעו ימיו למצות מילה is rendered literally; it refers to the practice of posthumous circumcision on a child who died before the eighth day."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:15.035441025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}